        "original_id": "1ef7ea76-0acd-56fd-afe0-1d0bcb941946",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Placido Rizzotto, Luciano Leggio\n- Roles: trade union leader, socialist peasant, Mafia boss, criminal\n- Organizations: Sicilian Mafia, Corleonesi\n- Places: Corleone\n\nFacts:\n- Placido Rizzotto was born in Corleone on January 2, 1914.\n- Luciano Leggio was born on January 6, 1925.\n- Placido Rizzotto was an Italian socialist peasant and trade union leader from Corleone.\n- Luciano Leggio was an Italian criminal and a leading figure of the Sicilian Mafia.\n- Luciano Leggio was the head of the Corleonesi, a Mafia faction that originated in the town of Corleone.\n- Placido Rizzotto was assassinated on March 10, 1948, by Sicilian Mafia boss Luciano Leggio.\n- Luciano Leggio died on November 15, 1993.",
